{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Used Car Price Estimator - Exploratory Data Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "EDA for the CarDekho **Car details v3** dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "The analysis covers price distribution, log price distribution, car age, kilometres driven, brand/fuel/transmission comparisons, and correlations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "PROJECT_ROOT = Path.cwd().parent\n",
    "if not (PROJECT_ROOT / 'data').exists():\n",
    "    PROJECT_ROOT = Path.cwd()\n",
    "\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, str(PROJECT_ROOT))\n",
    "\n",
    "from src.config import DATASET_PATH, IMG_DIR, CURRENT_YEAR\n",
    "\n",
    "IMG_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Dataset:', DATASET_PATH)\n",
    "print('Charts:', IMG_DIR)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df = pd.read_csv(DATASET_PATH)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Shape:', df.shape)\n",
    "display(df.head())\n    ",
    "print('\\nColumns:')\n",
    "print(df.columns.tolist())\n",
    "\n",
    "print('\\nMissing values:')\n",
    "display(df.isna().sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Basic feature engineering for EDA\n",
    "df['brand'] = df['name'].astype(str).str.strip().str.split().str[0]\n",
    "df['car_age'] = CURRENT_YEAR - df['year']\n",
    "\n",
    "for column in ['mileage', 'engine', 'max_power']:\n",
    "    df[column] = pd.to_numeric(\n",
    "        df[column].astype(str).str.extract(r'([-+]?\\d*\\.?\\d+)')[0],\n    "        errors='coerce'\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "df['log_price'] = np.log1p(df['selling_price'])\n",
    "\n",
    "display(df[['brand', 'car_age', 'selling_price', 'log_price', 'km_driven']].head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Selling Price Distribution\n",
    "\n",
    "**Insight:** The raw selling-price distribution shows how strongly used-car prices are concentrated and whether expensive cars create a long right tail."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "sns.histplot(df['selling_price'].dropna(), bins=50, kde=True)\n",
    "plt.title('Used Car Selling Price Distribution')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Selling Price (INR)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Number of Cars')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(IMG_DIR / 'price_distribution.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Log Price Distribution\n",
    "\n",
    "**Insight:** Applying `log1p` reduces the influence of very expensive vehicles and produces a more balanced target distribution for regression."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "sns.histplot(df['log_price'].dropna(), bins=50, kde=True)\n",
    "plt.title('Log-Transformed Selling Price Distribution')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('log1p(Selling Price)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Number of Cars')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(IMG_DIR / 'log_price_distribution.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Price vs Car Age\n",
    "\n",
    "**Insight:** This plot shows the relationship between vehicle age and resale price and helps identify depreciation patterns."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "sns.scatterplot(\n",
    "    data=df.sample(min(len(df), 5000), random_state=42),\n",
    "    x='car_age',\n",
    "    y='selling_price',\n",
    "    alpha=0.5\n",
    ")\n",
    "plt.title('Selling Price vs Car Age')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Car Age (years)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Selling Price (INR)')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(IMG_DIR / 'price_vs_age.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Price vs Kilometres Driven\n",
    "\n",
    "**Insight:** Higher kilometres driven can be associated with lower resale prices, although vehicle brand, age and specifications also contribute."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "sns.scatterplot(\n",
    "    data=df.sample(min(len(df), 5000), random_state=42),\n",
    "    x='km_driven',\n",
    "    y='selling_price',\n",
    "    alpha=0.5\n",
    ")\n",
    "plt.title('Selling Price vs Kilometres Driven')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Kilometres Driven')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Selling Price (INR)')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(IMG_DIR / 'price_vs_km.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Average Price by Brand\n",
    "\n",
    "**Insight:** Average resale prices differ substantially across brands, reflecting differences in vehicle segment, specifications and market demand."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "brand_prices = (\n",
    "    df.groupby('brand')['selling_price']\n",
    "      .mean()\n",
    "      .sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "      .head(15)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 7))\n",
    "sns.barplot(x=brand_prices.values, y=brand_prices.index)\n",
    "plt.title('Average Selling Price by Brand - Top 15')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Average Selling Price (INR)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Brand')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(IMG_DIR / 'avg_price_by_brand.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Average Price by Fuel Type\n",
    "\n",
    "**Insight:** Average resale price varies across fuel categories in the dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fuel_prices = df.groupby('fuel')['selling_price'].mean().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 6))\n",
    "sns.barplot(x=fuel_prices.index, y=fuel_prices.values)\n",
    "plt.title('Average Selling Price by Fuel Type')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Fuel Type')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Average Selling Price (INR)')\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=30)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(IMG_DIR / 'avg_price_by_fuel.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Average Price by Transmission\n",
    "\n",
    "**Insight:** Transmission type is associated with different average resale prices in this dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "transmission_prices = (\n",
    "    df.groupby('transmission')['selling_price']\n",
    "      .mean()\n",
    "      .sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(9, 6))\n",
    "sns.barplot(x=transmission_prices.index, y=transmission_prices.values)\n",
    "plt.title('Average Selling Price by Transmission')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Transmission')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Average Selling Price (INR)')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(IMG_DIR / 'avg_price_by_transmission.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Correlation Heatmap\n",
    "\n",
    "**Insight:** The correlation matrix helps identify numerical variables that have stronger linear relationships with selling price and with one another."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "correlation_columns = [\n",
    "    'selling_price',\n",
    "    'km_driven',\n",
    "    'year',\n",
    "    'car_age',\n",
    "    'mileage',\n",
    "    'engine',\n",
    "    'max_power',\n",
    "    'seats',\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "correlation = df[correlation_columns].corr(numeric_only=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(11, 8))\n",
    "sns.heatmap(correlation, annot=True, fmt='.2f', cmap='coolwarm', center=0)\n",
    "plt.title('Numerical Feature Correlation Heatmap')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig(IMG_DIR / 'correlation_heatmap.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "The EDA provides the foundation for preprocessing and model development. The regression model will predict resale price, while the classification model will use the predicted fair price and listed price to determine the deal category."
   ]
  }
 ],
